OpenFang Deployment Credentials
================================

Application URL: https://{{ openfang_domain }}/
API Endpoint: https://{{ openfang_domain }}/

API Authentication
==================
Bearer Token: {{ openfang_api_key }}

Example request:
  curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {{ openfang_api_key }}' https://{{ openfang_domain }}/api/status

Service Information
===================
Service Name: openfang.service (systemd)
Binary: {{ openfang_bin_path }}/openfang
Local API: {{ openfang_listen }} (loopback only; public access via NGINX)
Data Directory: {{ app_data_dir }}
Configuration File: {{ openfang_config_path }}

System Information
==================
Application User: {{ app_user }}
Application Home: {{ app_home }}
SSL Certificate: /etc/letsencrypt/live/{{ openfang_domain }}/

LLM Provider Setup
==================
OpenFang needs an LLM provider API key. Add it to the service environment
file at /etc/default/openfang, then restart the service:

  echo 'OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key' | sudo tee -a /etc/default/openfang
  sudo systemctl restart openfang

Supported provider variables:
  OpenAI:    OPENAI_API_KEY
  Anthropic: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
  Groq:      GROQ_API_KEY

Channel Adapters
================
Configure optional channel adapters in {{ openfang_config_path }}:

Telegram: bot_token_env = "TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"
Discord: bot_token_env = "DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN"
Slack: bot_token_env = "SLACK_BOT_TOKEN"

Useful Commands
===============
# Check service status
systemctl status openfang

# View service logs
journalctl -u openfang -f

# Restart OpenFang
systemctl restart openfang

# Test API connection
curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {{ openfang_api_key }}' https://{{ openfang_domain }}/api/status

For more information, visit: https://openfang.sh/docs/
